<Page
  title="About Bob Molina"
  description="SoftenerIndex is published by Bob Molina: an editorial hard-water directory that refuses invented numbers and door-to-door urgency."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Publisher</p>
      <h1>Bob Molina</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        SoftenerIndex is Molina’s public notebook for people who were just told they need a
        water softener — usually by someone already standing in the garage.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site’s job is narrow: explain what a fair quote contains, separate ion exchange
        from salt-free marketing, and keep city pages honest when the data file is still
        empty. It is not a dealer. It does not dispatch trucks. It does not invent a Phoenix
        hardness number to look finished.
      </p>
      <p>
        Affiliations, when they exist, will be labeled and routed through <a href="/go">/go</a>.
        Until then those destinations are placeholders. Editorial questions belong on the
        <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> page; advertising questions belong on the
        <a href="/disclosure">disclosure</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
